+# Lessons: billing
+
+### L-bill-1 Keep money as integer cents in src/billing; never round() floats
+- **Trigger:** editing money arithmetic in `src/billing/` (e.g. `total()` in `src/billing/total.py`, which today does `round(sum(i["price"] for i in items), 2)` on floats)
+- **Applies when:** prices or amounts are summed, compared, rounded or stored; store and compute in integer cents and convert only at the edge
+- **Doesn't apply when:** formatting cents into a display string for output (divide by 100 only there)
+- **Provenance:** user
+- **Date:** 2026-11-11
+- **Evidence:**
+```text
+User correction (2026-11-11), quoted:
+"Never use float money in src/billing. We store integer cents; round() on
+floats gave 10.299999 in the March invoice run (npm run invoices showed
+10.29 instead of 10.30)."
+
+Current code at src/billing/total.py:
+    def total(items):
+        return round(sum(i["price"] for i in items), 2)
+```
